# MadGraph5 batch script: g u > e+ e- u at LO, QCD=2 QED=2.
#
# One concrete flavour assignment out of the `g q > l+ l- q` class of
# `p p > l+ l- j QCD=2 QED=2` (MadGraph's P1_gq_llq group).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The first *mixed* incoming colour arrangement in the amplitude gate: one
#     coloured beam is a gluon (adjoint) and the other a quark (fundamental),
#     with the quark line running from the incoming quark through a spacelike
#     propagator to the outgoing quark. Every previously banked coloured
#     process has either two fundamental beams or two adjoint beams, so the
#     gluon-plus-quark initial state's colour-flow slot assignment and the
#     fermion flow through a spacelike line are unpinned before this row.
#   - Crossing of u u~ > e+ e- g, so its per-diagram amplitudes are the same
#     analytic functions at crossed momenta: a convention error that is a
#     property of the *arrangement* rather than of the functions shows up here
#     and not in the uux row.
#
# lpp=0 => fixed-energy partonic beams (g, u).
generate g u > e+ e- u QCD=2 QED=2
output gu_to_epemu -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
